From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PS3 Linux project <ps3@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:52:28 +0300
Subject: renderergl1: r_keepImages, the textures of image files kept across a
 map change

Every map load shut the renderer down and deleted every texture, then read, decoded and uploaded
each image file again, also when the next level was the same map: OpenArena's demo played in a
loop (games/bench) did that at every pass, 402 image files, and on the PS3 the reload is three
load-screen stalls of 340, 700 and 380 ms of main-thread CPU (pak4-textures.pk3 read and inflated,
the images decoded, compressed to DXT on the PPE): 10.2 of the run's 17.6 s of stalls. Players who
join during play (OpenArena adds a bot every 10 s) loaded their skins again in every pass too.
With r_keepImages 1 (default) RE_Shutdown without destroying the window moves the textures that
R_FindImageFile made from files to a list instead of deleting them, and R_FindImageFile takes one
back by name (same type and flags, else it loads the file again) before it reads the file. If the
next world is another map, RE_LoadWorldMap frees the list before that map loads its textures, as
upstream did; r_keepImages 2 keeps them across any map. RE_EndRegistration frees the kept textures
the new level didn't take back, except those the last level first used during play (players
joining), which stay until the level ends, for the same events in it. A renderer restart that
loads no world (a menu, the client restarting it twice on its way to a map) adds to the list. Any
setting that shapes a texture (picmip, texture bits, compression, texture mode, gamma...) or other
file system search paths free the list: qcommon sets fs_searchPathId, a hash of the search paths
(each pk3's checksum and file name, each directory) and of the pure server's pk3 list. A file
changed in a loose directory between levels needs vid_restart, which frees everything.
On llvmpipe the demo's reload went from 0.39-0.46 to 0.13-0.20 s (318 textures taken back), and the
joins' 23 uploads a pass from the second pass on to none; the frames are the same (66 screenshots
over three passes identical with cl_preloadLate, the random seed fixed).

diff --git a/code/qcommon/files.c b/code/qcommon/files.c
--- a/code/qcommon/files.c
+++ b/code/qcommon/files.c
@@ -3352,6 +3352,43 @@ static void FS_InitPathVars( void ) {
 	FS_AddPathVar( fs_microsoftstorepath );
 }
 
+/*
+================
+FS_UpdateSearchPathId
+
+fs_searchPathId: a hash of the search paths (each pk3's checksum and file name, each
+directory) and of the pure server's pk3 list, which decide where a file name is read
+from. renderer_opengl1's r_keepImages takes back no texture kept under another one.
+================
+*/
+static void FS_UpdateSearchPathId( void ) {
+	searchpath_t	*sp;
+	unsigned int	h = 5381;
+	const char		*c;
+	int				i;
+
+	for ( sp = fs_searchpaths ; sp ; sp = sp->next ) {
+		if ( sp->pack ) {
+			h = h * 33 ^ sp->pack->checksum;
+			c = sp->pack->pakFilename;
+		} else if ( sp->dir ) {
+			c = sp->dir->fullpath;
+		} else {
+			continue;
+		}
+		for ( ; *c ; c++ ) {
+			h = h * 33 ^ (unsigned char)*c;
+		}
+		h = h * 33 ^ '|';
+	}
+	h = h * 33 ^ fs_numServerPaks;
+	for ( i = 0 ; i < fs_numServerPaks ; i++ ) {
+		h = h * 33 ^ fs_serverPaks[i];
+	}
+	Cvar_Get( "fs_searchPathId", "0", CVAR_ROM );
+	Cvar_Set2( "fs_searchPathId", va( "%u", h ), qtrue );
+}
+
 /*
 ================
 FS_Startup
@@ -3455,6 +3492,8 @@ static void FS_Startup( const char *gameName )
 
 	fs_gamedirvar->modified = qfalse; // We just loaded, it's not modified
 
+	FS_UpdateSearchPathId();
+
 	Com_Printf( "----------------------\n" );
 
 #ifdef FS_MISSING
@@ -4013,6 +4052,7 @@ void FS_PureServerSetLoadedPaks( const char *pakSums, const char *pakNames ) {
 	for ( i = 0 ; i < c ; i++ ) {
 		fs_serverPaks[i] = atoi( Cmd_Argv( i ) );
 	}
+	FS_UpdateSearchPathId();
 
